49","rules":[{"id":"app-SuggestRemoteExecutionHint-OpNotSupportedByService","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Delegation warning. The highlighted part of this formula might not work correctly on large data sets. The \"{0}\" operation is not supported by this connector."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["If your data set exceeds the 500 record limit but contains less than 2,000 records, try resetting the limit.","Try simplifying the formula.","Try moving your data to a different data source."],"whyFix":"","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-SuggestRemoteExecutionHint","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Delegation warning. The \"{0}\" part of this formula might not work correctly on large data sets."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["If your data set exceeds the 500 record limit but contains less than 2,000 records, try resetting the limit.","Try simplifying the formula.","Try moving your data to a different data source."],"whyFix":"","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-SuggestRemoteExecutionHint-InOpRhs","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Delegation warning. The highlighted part of this formula might not work correctly on large data sets."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Change the item to the right of the \"in\" operator to be a column from the correct data source.","If your data set exceeds the 500 record limit but contains less than 2,000 records, try resetting the limit.","Try simplifying the formula.","Try moving your data to a different data source."],"whyFix":"","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-SuggestRemoteExecutionHint-OpNotSupportedByColumn","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Delegation warning. The highlighted part of this formula might not work correctly with column \"{0}\" on large data sets."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["If your data set exceeds the 500 record limit but contains less than 2,000 records, try resetting the limit.","Try simplifying the formula.","Try moving your data to a different data source."],"whyFix":"","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"acc-FocusBorderShouldBeVisible","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Focus isn't showing"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Change the FocusedBorderThickness property to be more than 0."],"whyFix":"If the focus isn't visible, people who don't use a mouse won't be able to see it when they're interacting with the app.","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"accessibility"}},{"id":"acc-TabIndexShouldBeDefinedForInteractiveControl","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Missing tab stop"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Set TabIndex to 0 or greater to ensure that interactive elements have a tab stop."],"whyFix":"People who use the keyboard with your app will not be able to access this element without a tab stop.","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"accessibility"}},{"id":"acc-AccessibleLabelNeeded","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Missing accessible label"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Edit the accessible label property to describe the item."],"whyFix":"If there's no accessible text, people who can’t see the screen won't understand what’s in images and controls.","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"accessibility"}},{"id":"app-CountRowsGalleryAllItems","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Use AllItemsCount instead of CountRows with AllItems"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Replace CountRows(Gallery.AllItems) with Gallery.AllItemsCount for better performance."],"whyFix":"Using CountRows with a gallery's AllItems property forces the creation of an output table containing a copy of the input data source and the current state of all child controls. This may force uninitialized rows to be initialized, consuming additional CPU cycles, memory, and potentially triggering row-level network requests.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}},{"id":"app-ForAllWithMutation","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Mutating a collection or data source inside ForAll may trigger excessive rule re-evaluation"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Since ForAll returns a table, pass its result as input to the mutation function in a single batched call. For example, replace ForAll(source, Collect(c, { ... })) with Collect(c, ForAll(source, { ... })); the same pattern applies to Patch and Remove. A single batched mutation emits one change notification instead of one per iteration.","For trivial per-row updates or deletions against a data source, prefer the delegable UpdateIf or RemoveIf functions called once outside ForAll instead of iterating with ForAll."],"whyFix":"Using Collect, Patch, Remove, or another mutation function inside the body of ForAll mutates the target collection or data source once per iteration. Every control property that depends on that collection or data source re-evaluates on each mutation, which can turn a small loop into thousands of rule evaluations and, for connected data sources, a network request per row.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}}]}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits"}]}